            "Second tier: osmotherapy with hypertonic saline or mannitol, deeper sedation with neuromuscular blockade if ventilator dyssynchrony contributes, cerebrospinal fluid drainage where a ventricular drain is present, and repeat imaging for a surgical lesion.",
            "Third tier: barbiturate coma, mild hypothermia or decompressive craniectomy — each with significant harms, so escalate with neurosurgical involvement and multimodal monitoring.",
