            "Hyperosmolar therapy: hypertonic saline 3% 2–5 mL/kg bolus (or continuous 0.1–1 mL/kg/h) targeting a sodium of about 145–155 mmol/L with osmolality below approximately 360 mosmol/L, or mannitol 0.25–1 g/kg; hypertonic saline is generally preferred in children, particularly if hypovolaemic.",
            "Second tier for refractory ICP: neuromuscular blockade, brief moderate hyperventilation to PaCO₂ 4.0–4.5 kPa as a temporary bridge only (with monitoring of brain oxygenation where possible), barbiturate coma with haemodynamic support, and early neurosurgical discussion about decompressive craniectomy or evacuation of the extradural collection. Steroids are not indicated.",
